From 1d6724e669f33bac407d2c43164c7fd9992acf99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:11:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: say why an interlaced or 3D Dolby Vision video
 plays without Dolby Vision

An interlaced or 3D Dolby Vision video is neither sent natively nor reconstructed: the bridge
takes progressive pictures of one view only (DVBRIDGE::Eligible(), ConversionEligible()). It
played from its base layer without a word in kodi.log. The line for a picture larger than native
output takes in was in DVBRIDGE::WantsNativeOutput(const CDVDStreamInfo&), which nothing calls,
so it was never written either; that overload is gone.

When a Dolby Vision video opens without native output (VideoPlayer, once a file), what in the
stream itself keeps the bridge from it (DVBRIDGE::StreamKeptOutOf(): interlaced, 3D, larger than
4096x2304) is now said once, and the user is then not told to change the display (the notice for
a display that offers Dolby Vision Low-Latency only), which would not bring Dolby Vision to that
video.

Where the renderer gives the bridge's pictures of a video up after two seconds of failures, for
the reconstruction or for the mapping to SDR, it said "its pictures could not be reconstructed"
(or mapped) also when the last one was a field, drawn alone because Kodi deinterlaces in the
renderer: that is now said as such (DVBRIDGE::RendererFailureReason()).
